    - type: 8
      name: 2
      line: 'I always loved that feeling when you walk down the quiet halls, where
        the lights are still on, all alone.


        Footsteps echoed off the sickly
        blue walls, and it''s hard to believe that just recently these halls were
        crowded with students.


        In complete silence, we slipped into the
        principal''s office; he wasn''t there.'
      font: 0
      inv: 0
